	<!-- ETCH TOOLS (2026-08-15). Replaces the fixed blunted pair in the spine, per the user:
	     NPC quarriers carry proper tools and the PLAYER keeps the blunted pair, which is what
	     makes the starter kit read as poverty rather than as the world's standard.
	     This is a weighted table rather than a {ownertier} ladder ON PURPOSE, and it is the one
	     place in the kit that does not scale. A per tier ladder needs a table for EVERY tier a
	     carver can spawn at, and a missing rung fails silently; with only two NPC rungs built,
	     weights give the same effect and cannot break. If the ladder ever grows, this is the line
	     that becomes Cleo_TerraFirma_EtchTools {ownertier}.
	     Chisel and mallet roll SEPARATELY, which is deliberate: the slip law takes the LESSER of
	     the two tiers, so a carver holding a carbide chisel and a steel mallet still carves at
	     steel. Mismatched pairs are a feature, not an oversight.
	     Carbide at 10 is a CLAUDE DRAFT weight, kept low because a tier-4 dagger is a 1d8 weapon
	     and a pack of them is a different fight from a pack of quarriers.
	     2026-08-22: the mod's steel/carbide chisel+mallet quartet DELETED (user ruling, knives
	     and hammers in their place); these are now the base blueprints directly. The slip law
	     reads skill + tier, so nothing else changes. -->
	<population Name="Cleo_TerraFirma_EtchTools">
		<group Name="Tools" Style="pickeach">
			<group Name="Edge" Style="pickone">
				<object Weight="90" Blueprint="Steel Dagger" Number="1" />
				<object Weight="10" Blueprint="Dagger4" Number="1" />
			</group>
			<group Name="Striker" Style="pickone">
				<object Weight="90" Blueprint="Steel Hammer" Number="1" />
				<object Weight="10" Blueprint="Cudgel4" Number="1" />
			</group>
		</group>
	</population>
